951
01:14:58.276 --> 01:15:00.471
[LlNE RlNGlNG]

952
01:15:03.080 --> 01:15:04.104
Hello?

953
01:15:04.282 --> 01:15:06.307
-Hey, it's me.
-Hey.

954
01:15:07.518 --> 01:15:09.179
What's going on?

955
01:15:09.353 --> 01:15:12.584
I don't know if I can
do this anymore, sissy.

956
01:15:13.691 --> 01:15:15.955
It's gonna be okay.

957
01:15:16.127 --> 01:15:18.561
Do you hear me? I promise.

958
01:15:18.729 --> 01:15:20.924
Who you talking to? Hello?

959
01:15:21.666 --> 01:15:23.099
Hello?

960
01:15:29.941 --> 01:15:34.640
Mrs. Fitzgerald, how old was Anna
when she started donating to her sister?

961
01:15:34.812 --> 01:15:36.211
She was a newborn.

962
01:15:36.380 --> 01:15:39.042
And at 5, she started donating lymphocytes,
is that correct?

963
01:15:39.217 --> 01:15:40.241
Mm-hm.

964
01:15:40.418 --> 01:15:42.386
-What does that involve?
-Giving blood.

965
01:15:42.553 --> 01:15:45.113
-Did Anna agree to that?
-No, she was 5.

966
01:15:45.289 --> 01:15:48.281
So you didn't ask her if they could
stick the needles in her arm?

967
01:15:49.026 --> 01:15:51.494
I asked her to help her sister,
and she agreed.

968
01:15:51.662 --> 01:15:52.720
Really?

969
01:15:52.897 --> 01:15:56.355
Didn't two nurses have to hold Anna down
because she was fighting so hard?

970
01:15:56.534 --> 01:15:57.523
Mm-hm.

971
01:15:57.702 --> 01:16:00.296
So she didn't completely agree,
now, did she?

972
01:16:00.471 --> 01:16:03.872
Mr. Alexander, it's just us chickens.
No showboating, please.

973
01:16:04.041 --> 01:16:06.771
I'm sorry, Your Honor. Force of habit.

974
01:16:07.211 --> 01:16:13.150
Mrs. Fitzgerald, how old was Anna
the next time she was hospitalized?

975
01:16:13.751 --> 01:16:16.379
-When Kate was 9, she got a--
-That's not what I asked.

976
01:16:16.554 --> 01:16:21.287
I want to find out what happened
to Anna when she was 6.

977
01:16:23.527 --> 01:16:26.428
-She donated granulocytes.
-And what's that? More needles?

978
01:16:26.597 --> 01:16:27.621
Yup.

979
01:16:27.798 --> 01:16:31.529
And did you ask Anna if she was willing
to donate the granulocytes?

980
01:16:31.702 --> 01:16:33.932
Her sister needed them.
She was the only match.

981
01:16:34.105 --> 01:16:35.732
But did you ask her?

982
01:16:42.647 --> 01:16:45.207
Mrs. Fitzgerald,
answer the question, please.

983
01:16:47.952 --> 01:16:49.852
No, I didn't.

984
01:16:50.288 --> 01:16:53.917
We talked about it a lot, but no,
I didn't ask her permission.

985
01:16:54.992 --> 01:16:58.052
Next was the bone-marrow aspiration.

986
01:16:58.229 --> 01:17:01.892
Could you describe
that procedure for us?

987
01:17:02.667 --> 01:17:04.931
They put needles into Anna's hips.

988
01:17:05.102 --> 01:17:07.502
-lnto the bone? Big needles?
-Yes. Mm-hm.

989
01:17:07.672 --> 01:17:12.166
Using your hands, would you indicate
to the court the size of those needles?

990
01:17:17.715 --> 01:17:21.242
It's a tough procedure, am I right?
Anna had to be hospitalized afterward.

991
01:17:21.419 --> 01:17:23.080
SARA: Yes.
CAMPBELL: For how long?

992
01:17:23.254 --> 01:17:27.088
Six days.
There were some complications.

993
01:17:27.258 --> 01:17:28.782
I see.

994
01:17:29.093 --> 01:17:31.527
You add it all up,
it's not so innocuous, is it?

995
01:17:31.696 --> 01:17:33.789
It's tough to hear
it all hashed out that way.

996
01:17:33.964 --> 01:17:37.559
I don't see the point. Court's well aware
of the family's medical history.

997
01:17:37.735 --> 01:17:40.431
Of Kate's history, Your Honor,
but not of Anna's.

998
01:17:40.604 --> 01:17:42.504
Fair enough. Proceed.

999
01:18:23.414 --> 01:18:28.044
Mrs. Fitzgerald, looking back and only
taking into account Anna's well-being...

1000
01:18:28.219 --> 01:18:32.280
...do you think it's reasonable to conclude
that you might have taken this too far?

1001
01:18:40.331 --> 01:18:44.631
Looking at only Anna's situation...

1002
01:18:44.802 --> 01:18:47.737
...yes, it is.

1003
01:18:47.905 --> 01:18:49.873
But I have to think about
my entire family.

1004
01:18:50.040 --> 01:18:51.701
-But Kate comes first?
-Kate's sick.

1005
01:18:51.876 --> 01:18:54.208
So this is a triage situation.

1006
01:18:54.378 --> 01:18:57.745
Compromising one child's health
on behalf of the other. Where's the line?

1007
01:18:57.915 --> 01:19:00.440
-For Kate, it's life or death.
-Not for Kate, for Anna.

1008
01:19:00.618 --> 01:19:02.813
-She's why we're here.
-That's a trick question.

1009
01:19:02.987 --> 01:19:05.751
Because Anna
isn't the only person in this equation.

1010
01:19:05.923 --> 01:19:09.757
And if we were looking at it only from
Anna's situation, sure, it is brutal.

1011
01:19:09.927 --> 01:19:14.057
I mean, who wants to be stuck
and poked and prodded by needles?

1012
01:19:14.231 --> 01:19:17.997
And you can look at me and you can say
how awful I am for doing that to my child.

1013
01:19:18.169 --> 01:19:22.162
You know what? It is awful. But it's not
as awful as putting your child in the ground.

1014
01:19:22.339 --> 01:19:24.330
-You stand up for your family.
-It's my job.

1015
01:19:24.508 --> 01:19:26.066
-And you stand up for Kate.
-I do.

1016
01:19:26.243 --> 01:19:28.302
But the real question is:

1017
01:19:28.813 --> 01:19:30.906
Who stands up for Anna?

1018
01:19:36.187 --> 01:19:37.950
Nothing further, Your Honor.

1019
01:19:42.359 --> 01:19:44.384
[DOG BARKlNG]

1020
01:19:46.730 --> 01:19:49.563
Mr. Alexander,
does your dog have to go to the bathroom?

1021
01:19:49.733 --> 01:19:51.598
No, Your Honor, but I may need a recess.

1022
01:19:51.769 --> 01:19:55.569
I'm afraid that's out of the question.
I wanna finish today. Next witness, please.

1023
01:19:55.739 --> 01:19:58.071
The court calls Anna Fitzgerald.

1024
01:19:58.242 --> 01:20:00.403
[DOG WHlMPERlNG AND BARKlNG]

1025
01:20:01.912 --> 01:20:05.075
I mean it. If you can't control your animal,
I'll have him removed.

1026
01:20:05.249 --> 01:20:06.580
-Quiet, Judge.
-Excuse me?

1027
01:20:06.750 --> 01:20:09.651
No, no, I was speaking to the dog.
The dog's name is Judge.

1028
01:20:09.820 --> 01:20:13.051
I don't care what his name is,
I want him quiet.

1029
01:20:13.224 --> 01:20:14.282
BAlLlFF:
Raise your hand.

1030
01:20:14.458 --> 01:20:17.086
Do you swear to tell the truth,
whole truth, nothing but the truth?

1031
01:20:17.261 --> 01:20:19.593
-Yup.
-Please state your name for the record.

1032
01:20:19.763 --> 01:20:21.230
Anna Fitzgerald.

1033
01:20:25.469 --> 01:20:27.960
-Hey, Mom.
-Hi, sweetheart.

1034
01:20:29.240 --> 01:20:32.676
You wanna tell us why we're here?
Why you're doing this?

1035
01:20:33.210 --> 01:20:34.837
For medical emancipation.

1036
01:20:35.279 --> 01:20:36.576
SARA:
That's not what I mean.

1037
01:20:36.747 --> 01:20:38.442
You love your sister, right?

1038
01:20:38.883 --> 01:20:41.613
You know she's sick.
Why won't you help her?

1039
01:20:44.655 --> 01:20:46.316
[PHlL X'S "KlLL ME"
PLAYlNG OVER SPEAKERS]

1040
01:20:46.490 --> 01:20:48.958
What are you doing in there?

1041
01:20:49.126 --> 01:20:50.684
[THUDDlNG AND CLATTERlNG]

1042
01:20:51.529 --> 01:20:54.396
Come on, Kate, just let me in!

1043
01:20:58.502 --> 01:21:01.369
What's going on?
It smells like booze in here.

1044
01:21:01.539 --> 01:21:03.632
-Having a little party.
-A party?

1045
01:21:03.807 --> 01:21:07.174
Yeah, a going-away party.

1046
01:21:09.313 --> 01:21:13.272
See you, Mom!
Goodbye, fucking hospital!

1047
01:21:13.450 --> 01:21:14.974
Damn!

1048
01:21:15.853 --> 01:21:18.253
What are you doing?

1049
01:21:18.422 --> 01:21:19.980
I'm going to see Taylor.

1050
01:21:20.157 --> 01:21:23.251
What? No! No!

1051
01:21:23.527 --> 01:21:25.256
No!

1052
01:21:25.462 --> 01:21:28.226
So you're here for medical emancipation?

1053
01:21:28.766 --> 01:21:30.427
Right.

1054
01:21:37.041 --> 01:21:38.508
Yes.

1055
01:21:40.177 --> 01:21:41.838
Is that it?

1056
01:21:42.446 --> 01:21:45.574
-ls that the only reason?
-That's the only reason.

1057
01:21:45.749 --> 01:21:47.011
Are you sure?

1058
01:21:47.184 --> 01:21:50.415
Hold, please. Mr. Fitzgerald,
is there something you wanted to say?

1059
01:21:50.588 --> 01:21:52.522
I don't know, is there?

1060
01:21:52.690 --> 01:21:53.714
BRlAN:
Hey.

1061
01:21:53.891 --> 01:21:54.880
[DOG BARKlNG]

1062
01:21:55.059 --> 01:21:56.754
Okay. All right, that is the last time.

1063
01:21:56.927 --> 01:22:00.590
If you do not control him, I'm going to
have the bailiff remove him. I mean it.

1064
01:22:00.764 --> 01:22:03.790
CAMPBELL: Your Honor--
DE SALVO: Not another word, counselor.

1065
01:22:03.968 --> 01:22:05.401
Proceed, please.

1066
01:22:05.569 --> 01:22:08.800
-I just want to be in charge of my own body.
JESSE: No, you don't.

1067
01:22:09.907 --> 01:22:10.931
Down.

1068
01:22:11.108 --> 01:22:15.875
-You want me to do something about this?
-No, leave it. It's kind of interesting.

1069
01:22:19.350 --> 01:22:21.045
Okay, so you want to be in charge.

1070
01:22:21.218 --> 01:22:24.210
Yeah. It's my body, I want to be able
to make my own decisions...

1071
01:22:24.388 --> 01:22:26.356
...about what to do with it.

1072
01:22:29.393 --> 01:22:33.796
No. No, I know you, Anna Fitzgerald,
and that's not it.

1073
01:22:33.964 --> 01:22:35.124
It doesn't add up.

1074
01:22:35.299 --> 01:22:37.597
For a week now
you've been avoiding the question.

1075
01:22:37.768 --> 01:22:41.568
"l can't tell you." "I'm sorry."
"l don't wanna talk about it."

1076
01:22:41.739 --> 01:22:44.003
You've been walking around
like nothing's wrong...

1077
01:22:44.174 --> 01:22:46.267
...while your sister rots in that hospital!

1078
01:22:46.443 --> 01:22:48.934
-I don't wanna do it anymore.
-I don't believe you.

1079
01:22:49.113 --> 01:22:51.240
-You are hiding something, Anna.
-I'm not.

1080
01:22:51.415 --> 01:22:53.610
People give their kidneys
to total strangers.

1081
01:22:53.784 --> 01:22:56.218
-You'd better start talking right now.
ANNA: I'm talking!

1082
01:22:56.387 --> 01:22:58.412
-You start telling me the truth.
-I am!

1083
01:22:58.589 --> 01:23:00.955
You're not.
Because if you are, I don't know you.

1084
01:23:01.125 --> 01:23:03.719
-Jesus Christ, Anna, just tell them.
-You shut up!

1085
01:23:03.894 --> 01:23:06.294
-Tell them!
-You promised me you wouldn't do this!

1086
01:23:06.463 --> 01:23:07.487
JESSE:
Tell them!

1087
01:23:07.665 --> 01:23:09.462
-God, you people are so stupid!
ANNA: You promised!

1088
01:23:09.633 --> 01:23:11.225
-Kate wants to die!
ANNA: Stop it!

1089
01:23:15.272 --> 01:23:18.605
She's making Anna do all this
because she knows she's not gonna survive.

1090
01:23:18.776 --> 01:23:20.903
-That's a lie, Jesse!
-Oh, no, it's not!

1091
01:23:21.078 --> 01:23:22.943
Kate's dying and everybody knows it.

1092
01:23:23.113 --> 01:23:25.877
You just love her so much
that you don't want to let her go.

1093
01:23:26.050 --> 01:23:27.074
Your Honor?

1094
01:23:27.251 --> 01:23:29.776
But it's time, Mom. Kate's ready.

1095
01:23:31.055 --> 01:23:33.148
That's not true.

1096
01:23:33.557 --> 01:23:34.785
Kate would have told me.

1097
01:23:34.958 --> 01:23:38.223
-Your Honor, l--
-Mom, she did tell you.

1098
01:23:38.395 --> 01:23:39.987
BRlAN:
She did.

1099
01:23:40.431 --> 01:23:43.491
She told you a million times.
You didn't wanna hear it.

1100
01:23:53.377 --> 01:23:54.708
Mr. Alexander.

1101
01:23:55.546 --> 01:23:58.515
Mr. Alexander.

1102
01:24:09.860 --> 01:24:11.623
ANNA:
Right then, I understood the real reason...

1103
01:24:11.795 --> 01:24:15.094
...why Campbell Alexander
took on my case.

1104
01:24:15.265 --> 01:24:17.733
It wasn't for the notoriety.

1105
01:24:17.901 --> 01:24:20.199
He was an epileptic.

1106
01:24:20.537 --> 01:24:23.597
He knew what it was like
to not have control over his own body.

1107
01:24:23.774 --> 01:24:25.002
KATE:
Anna?

1108
01:24:27.711 --> 01:24:29.542
Sissy.

1109
01:24:32.349 --> 01:24:34.010
Oh, my God.

1110
01:24:34.184 --> 01:24:35.981
Oh, my God.

1111
01:24:55.739 --> 01:24:57.001
KATE:
Don't worry.

1112
01:24:57.174 --> 01:25:00.632
It's just the new medicine
getting ready for the kidney.

1113
01:25:02.746 --> 01:25:04.407
You in pain?

1114
01:25:04.581 --> 01:25:06.139
Pain?

1115
01:25:07.084 --> 01:25:09.484
My whole life is a pain.

1116
01:25:23.433 --> 01:25:25.924
This is the end, sissy.

1117
01:25:27.604 --> 01:25:30.630
It just gets scarier from here on out.

1118
01:25:33.143 --> 01:25:36.078
Mom's gonna chop me and cut me...

1119
01:25:37.114 --> 01:25:39.412
...till I'm a vegetable.

1120
01:25:42.886 --> 01:25:47.516
Two cells in a Petri dish
that she shocks with an electric cord.

1121
01:25:47.958 --> 01:25:49.789
You'll be all right.

1122
01:25:53.997 --> 01:25:55.828
It's over.

1123
01:25:56.266 --> 01:25:57.460
Time to go.

1124
01:26:04.408 --> 01:26:07.809
I need you to do me a favor, sissy.

1125
01:26:09.713 --> 01:26:11.305
What favor?

1126
01:26:13.317 --> 01:26:15.785
You can release me.

1127
01:26:25.596 --> 01:26:28.394
Are you certain you don't wanna
take the rest of the day off?

1128
01:26:28.565 --> 01:26:30.965
Oh, no, Your Honor. I'm fine.

1129
01:26:31.368 --> 01:26:33.996
Anything for a recess, right?

1130
01:26:37.074 --> 01:26:39.304
So, Anna, for the record.

1131
01:26:39.476 --> 01:26:43.606
Did you tell Kate you would stop
being a donor so that she could die?

1132
01:26:44.047 --> 01:26:46.709
-Yeah.
-And what did she say?

1133
01:26:49.853 --> 01:26:51.377
ANNA:
Mom and Dad are gonna kill me.

1134
01:26:51.822 --> 01:26:53.722
What am I supposed to tell them?

1135
01:26:53.891 --> 01:26:56.325
KATE:
Tell them you're important too.

1136
01:26:56.860 --> 01:26:58.885
Tell them you wanna play soccer.

1137
01:26:59.062 --> 01:27:01.428
Tell them you wanna cheerlead.

1138
01:27:01.598 --> 01:27:03.065
They'll never believe me.

1139
01:27:03.233 --> 01:27:04.962
Yeah, they will.

1140
01:27:05.636 --> 01:27:07.695
And you wanna know why?

1141
01:27:08.872 --> 01:27:10.806
Because it's the truth.

1142
01:27:11.575 --> 01:27:14.703
ANNA: Oh, boy.
-I know.

1143
01:27:21.118 --> 01:27:22.915
ANNA:
You scared?

1144
01:27:23.820 --> 01:27:27.085
No. I know I'll be okay.

1145
01:27:29.192 --> 01:27:31.558
What do you think happens?

1146
01:27:31.895 --> 01:27:35.626
I mean, where do you go?

1147
01:27:36.667 --> 01:27:38.726
I don't know, baby.

1148
01:27:40.470 --> 01:27:42.404
But who knows?

1149
01:27:44.374 --> 01:27:46.899
Wherever it is, maybe I'll run into Taylor.

1150
01:27:49.713 --> 01:27:51.510
Will you wait for me?

1151
01:27:51.682 --> 01:27:53.309
What?

1152
01:27:53.483 --> 01:27:57.180
If you go anywhere crazy, will you wait?

1153
01:27:57.354 --> 01:28:01.848
I mean, how will I know
how to find you?

1154
01:28:04.161 --> 01:28:07.619
If you're ever lost or scared...

1155
01:28:07.798 --> 01:28:09.561
...go to Montana.

1156
01:28:10.167 --> 01:28:12.397
-Montana?
-Yeah.

1157
01:28:13.136 --> 01:28:15.036
That's where I'll be.

1158
01:28:17.541 --> 01:28:19.099
ANNA:
Okay.

1159
01:28:20.477 --> 01:28:22.945
What did she say, Anna?

1160
01:28:23.880 --> 01:28:25.404
She said, "Thanks."

1161
01:28:29.753 --> 01:28:31.880
All right,
I think I have enough information...

1162
01:28:32.055 --> 01:28:35.650
...but before I make my decision,
I'd like to visit Kate, if that's all right.

1163
01:28:39.062 --> 01:28:44.591
It's hard to say. It takes from anywhere
between 24 and 48 hours or so.

1164
01:28:56.380 --> 01:28:58.746
WOMAN [OVER SPEAKERS] :
Radiology therapist to Room 231.

1165
01:28:58.915 --> 01:29:02.612
Radiology therapist to Room 231.

1166
01:29:23.140 --> 01:29:25.005
PERVlS: Hey, sweetheart. How you feeling?
-Hey.

1167
01:29:25.175 --> 01:29:26.267
-Hi.
-Hi, sweetie.

1168
01:29:26.443 --> 01:29:29.207
-Hi. Hey, you look good. You do.
-Hi.

1169
01:29:29.379 --> 01:29:30.846
Look, I got you this book, okay?

1170
01:29:31.014 --> 01:29:33.915
It's full of guided meditations,
visualizations, healing stuff.

1171
01:29:34.084 --> 01:29:36.052
-Really good for you, okay?
-Okay.

1172
01:29:36.219 --> 01:29:37.311
-Hey.
-Hi.

1173
01:29:37.487 --> 01:29:38.613
-Keep fighting.
-Okay.

1174
01:29:38.789 --> 01:29:40.279
A lot of living to do, okay?

1175
01:29:42.292 --> 01:29:43.759
-All right, promise me?
-Promise.

1176
01:29:43.927 --> 01:29:46.293
-Promise?
-Promise.

1177
01:29:48.131 --> 01:29:52.465
Hey, you let the cat out of the bag,
you naughty boy.

1178
01:29:52.636 --> 01:29:54.934
I didn't know what else to do.

1179
01:29:57.174 --> 01:30:00.166
-I'm sorry.
-Hey.

1180
01:30:00.710 --> 01:30:03.873
Hey, you know what you did?

1181
01:30:08.452 --> 01:30:10.249
You know how brave you are?

1182
01:30:25.068 --> 01:30:28.162
-How about some pizza?
-I'm up for that.

1183
01:30:28.338 --> 01:30:30.329
-Definitely. Definitely.
PERVlS: Yeah.

1184
01:30:30.507 --> 01:30:32.031
TOMMY'S WlFE: Good timing.
-I'll get the pizza.

1185
01:30:32.209 --> 01:30:35.235
ELLEN: Yeah, Anna wants a slice.
KELLY: I'm just gonna pass it out.

1186
01:30:35.412 --> 01:30:37.209
-There's cheese--
TOMMY: There's an idea.

1187
01:30:37.380 --> 01:30:38.745
KELLY:
And pepperoni and everything.

1188
01:30:38.915 --> 01:30:40.542
TOMMY'S WlFE:
You guys want cheese, right?

1189
01:30:40.717 --> 01:30:43.709
SARA: Anna wants a piece.
TOMMY'S WlFE: Of cheese, pepperoni?

1190
01:30:43.887 --> 01:30:47.914
ANNA: I want pizza and 7UP.
Thank you.

1191
01:30:49.659 --> 01:30:52.526
You've just gotta tell yourself
you're gonna get better.

1192
01:30:52.696 --> 01:30:56.393
Tell your brain to heal yourself
and work on it while you're sleeping.

1193
01:30:56.566 --> 01:30:58.625
-Okay.
-I'm not kidding.

1194
01:30:58.802 --> 01:31:00.235
-No, I will. I promise.
-Okay.

1195
01:31:00.403 --> 01:31:02.530
Subconscious mind
is a really powerful thing.

1196
01:31:02.706 --> 01:31:05.470
Yeah, you know,
it's like this lady I saw on TV.

1197
01:31:05.642 --> 01:31:09.203
She would talk to her cancer cells
and ask them to go away.

1198
01:31:09.379 --> 01:31:12.314
And eventually they did.
I did not make this up, this is true.

1199
01:31:12.482 --> 01:31:14.814
-"Go away, cancer cells."
TOMMY'S WlFE: Yeah, like that.

1200
01:31:14.985 --> 01:31:17.419
-"Out."
-Speaking more sincerely than that.

1201
01:31:17.587 --> 01:31:20.818
TOMMY: What about that prisoner story?
Prisoners are in there for 10 years...

1202
01:31:20.991 --> 01:31:25.291
...and practicing their invisible golf swing.
They practice, and see it in their mind...

1203
01:31:25.462 --> 01:31:28.920
...so by the time they get out, boom,
they're scratch golfers.

1204
01:31:29.099 --> 01:31:31.363
It's true.
I've even heard about those mothers...

1205
01:31:31.535 --> 01:31:33.435
...the ones who get supernatural power...

1206
01:31:33.603 --> 01:31:36.504
...and they can lift up a car
and save their babies. It's amazing.

1207
01:31:36.673 --> 01:31:39.073
TOMMY'S WlFE: Miracles happen every day.
PERVlS: That's right.

1208
01:31:39.242 --> 01:31:41.233
This world isn't
made up of science and medicine.

1209
01:31:41.411 --> 01:31:45.313
There are powerful things out there
that none of us can understand.

1210
01:31:45.515 --> 01:31:47.506
TOMMY: Read the book.
KELLY: There's more over here.

1211
01:31:47.684 --> 01:31:50.380
SARA: We'll read the book.
KATE: I promise, I'll read the book.

1212
01:31:54.090 --> 01:31:56.786
Sorry, guys, everybody's gotta go.
Visiting hours are over.

1213
01:31:56.960 --> 01:32:00.225
-Seriously, out.
TOMMY'S WlFE: We just got here.

1214
01:32:00.397 --> 01:32:02.888
TOMMY: We just gotta eat.
I'm personally starving.

1215
01:32:03.066 --> 01:32:05.159
TOMMY'S WlFE:
See you really soon, okay?

1216
01:32:06.736 --> 01:32:09.136
[MUTED DlALOGUE]

1217
01:32:19.216 --> 01:32:20.547
[MOUTHS]
Come on.

1218
01:32:29.659 --> 01:32:31.593
KATE:
Hey, guys?

1219
01:32:31.761 --> 01:32:35.162
I love you all, but could you go home?

1220
01:32:35.332 --> 01:32:37.857
I need some time with Mom.

1221
01:32:40.136 --> 01:32:41.535
Yeah.

1222
01:32:43.139 --> 01:32:44.333
Yeah.

1223
01:32:44.507 --> 01:32:46.236
Let's go. Come on.

1224
01:32:46.910 --> 01:32:49.208
[WHlSPERlNG lNDlSTlNCTLY]

1225
01:33:18.108 --> 01:33:19.666
You don't wanna talk?

1226
01:33:20.310 --> 01:33:21.971
Nope.

1227
01:33:24.848 --> 01:33:26.076
KATE:
Are you mad at me?

1228
01:33:26.249 --> 01:33:28.911
I'm not mad at you, I'm just mad.

1229
01:33:29.452 --> 01:33:31.818
You gotta get some rest, okay?

1230
01:33:32.455 --> 01:33:34.787
You be strong for surgery.

1231
01:33:46.136 --> 01:33:48.536
I made this for you.

1232
01:33:50.707 --> 01:33:52.436
What is it?

1233
01:33:53.677 --> 01:33:55.838
It's everything.

1234
01:33:56.346 --> 01:33:57.574
It's us.

1235
01:35:28.004 --> 01:35:30.598
It was a good one, wasn't it?

1236
01:35:31.841 --> 01:35:33.308
The best.

1237
01:35:41.251 --> 01:35:46.245
Remember that summer
when I went away to camp?

1238
01:35:46.689 --> 01:35:49.419
And I was so scared
that I'd miss you guys.

1239
01:35:49.592 --> 01:35:52.527
-Yeah.
-Before I got on the bus...

1240
01:35:52.695 --> 01:35:55.687
...you told me to take a seat
on the left side...

1241
01:35:55.865 --> 01:35:57.560
...right next to the window...

1242
01:35:57.734 --> 01:36:01.192
...so I'd be able to look back
and see you there.

1243
01:36:04.474 --> 01:36:06.442
I remember.

1244
01:36:09.479 --> 01:36:12.107
I get the same seat now.

1245
01:36:15.285 --> 01:36:17.515
It's gonna be okay.

1246
01:36:17.687 --> 01:36:20.588
[SOBBlNG]

1247
01:36:26.696 --> 01:36:29.164
It's gonna be okay, Mom.

1248
01:36:29.866 --> 01:36:31.959
I promise.

1249
01:36:45.548 --> 01:36:47.948
ANNA:
My sister died that night.

1250
01:36:50.420 --> 01:36:53.981
I wish I could say
that she made some miracle recovery...

1251
01:36:54.157 --> 01:36:55.920
...but she didn't.

1252
01:36:56.726 --> 01:36:58.956
She just stopped breathing.

1253
01:37:08.805 --> 01:37:13.139
[MUTED DlALOGUE]

1254
01:37:31.427 --> 01:37:35.420
And I wish I could tell you that there was
some good that came out of it...

1255
01:37:35.798 --> 01:37:39.234
...that through Kate's death
we could all go on living.

1256
01:37:39.402 --> 01:37:42.735
Or even that her life
had some special meaning...

1257
01:37:43.039 --> 01:37:46.805
...Iike they named a park after her,
or a street...

1258
01:37:46.976 --> 01:37:50.537
...or that the Supreme Court
changed a law because of her.

1259
01:37:51.948 --> 01:37:53.779
But none of that happened.

1260
01:37:54.751 --> 01:37:56.616
She's just gone...

1261
01:37:56.786 --> 01:37:59.346
...a little piece of blue sky now.

1262
01:37:59.522 --> 01:38:01.752
And we all have to move on.

1263
01:38:05.261 --> 01:38:07.320
[KNOCKlNG]

1264
01:38:13.536 --> 01:38:16.164
A few days later, I got a surprise visitor.

1265
01:38:19.609 --> 01:38:21.099
Hi.

1266
01:38:22.345 --> 01:38:24.336
Somebody here wants to see you.

1267
01:38:24.514 --> 01:38:26.141
[BARKlNG]

1268
01:38:28.217 --> 01:38:30.151
ANNA:
Hey, Judge.

1269
01:38:31.187 --> 01:38:32.711
Hello.

1270
01:38:38.761 --> 01:38:39.853
I brought this for you.

1271
01:38:51.240 --> 01:38:52.867
We won.

1272
01:38:55.445 --> 01:38:59.506
You still have to do your homework and
go to bed when your parents tell you to...

1273
01:38:59.682 --> 01:39:02.742
...but you're now officially
medically emancipated.

1274
01:39:04.287 --> 01:39:06.221
Ninety-percent success rate, right?

1275
01:39:07.290 --> 01:39:09.019
Ninety-one.

1276
01:39:16.699 --> 01:39:18.166
Well...

1277
01:39:19.302 --> 01:39:21.270
...I suppose I should go.

1278
01:39:33.416 --> 01:39:37.147
Thanks for stopping by, Mr. A.
It was really good to see you.

1279
01:39:37.854 --> 01:39:39.481
You too.

1280
01:39:43.926 --> 01:39:46.622
If there's ever anything else you need...

1281
01:39:47.096 --> 01:39:48.120
...you know?

1282
01:39:49.232 --> 01:39:50.324
Okay.

1283
01:39:52.735 --> 01:39:54.293
Judge.

1284
01:40:18.895 --> 01:40:20.988
ANNA:
Life is different now.

1285
01:40:22.031 --> 01:40:25.159
A lot has changed in the last few years.

1286
01:40:25.401 --> 01:40:28.893
Mom went back to work,
rebuilt her practice...

1287
01:40:29.072 --> 01:40:32.007
...and is now making a very nice living.

1288
01:40:33.309 --> 01:40:34.799
Dad took an early pension...

1289
01:40:34.977 --> 01:40:38.538
...and now spends time
counseling troubled inner-city youths.

1290
01:40:40.817 --> 01:40:43.377
And Jesse's doing best of all.

1291
01:40:44.420 --> 01:40:47.947
After Kate died, he turned his life around.

1292
01:40:48.124 --> 01:40:49.682
He went back to school...

1293
01:40:49.859 --> 01:40:54.592
...and got himself a scholarship
to a fancy art academy in New York.

1294
01:40:58.367 --> 01:41:01.268
And even though we've grown up
and moved away...

1295
01:41:01.437 --> 01:41:06.067
...every year, on Kate's birthday,
we all take a vacation together...

1296
01:41:06.242 --> 01:41:09.006
...and it's always to the same place.

1297
01:41:43.012 --> 01:41:47.415
I'll never understand why Kate
had to die and we all got to live.

1298
01:41:49.318 --> 01:41:51.786
There's no reason for it, I guess.

1299
01:41:52.221 --> 01:41:56.555
Death's just death,
nobody understands it.

1300
01:42:42.371 --> 01:42:43.770
Once upon a time...

1301
01:42:44.507 --> 01:42:47.999
...I thought I was put on Earth
to save my sister.

1302
01:42:49.178 --> 01:42:52.841
And in the end, I couldn't do it.

1303
01:42:53.549 --> 01:42:55.744
I realize now...

1304
01:42:55.918 --> 01:42:57.545
... that wasn't the point.

1305
01:42:57.720 --> 01:43:00.154
The point was, I had a sister.

1306
01:43:00.323 --> 01:43:02.723
She was fantastic.

1307
01:43:05.161 --> 01:43:07.789
One day, I'm sure I'll see her again.

1308
01:43:08.831 --> 01:43:10.765
But until then...

1309
01:43:11.000 --> 01:43:13.867
...our relationship continues.
